# ── Site ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public origin, used to build the absolute URLs in Open Graph and canonical
# tags. Without it they are built against http://localhost:3000, so a link
# shared from production would point at the developer's own machine.
SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Must be a REPLICA SET: order confirm and dispatch run inside transactions.
MONGODB_URI="mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/nutridrip"

# ── Sessions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# At least 16 characters, or the app refuses to start in production.
JWT_SECRET="change-me-in-production-please-use-32-chars-min"
SESSION_EXPIRY_HOURS="24"

# ── Address lookup (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these, the address form still works: the patient types the address and
# can contribute coordinates from their device. With them, they get address
# search and a draggable pin, and city/pincode fill themselves in.
#
# Coordinates matter beyond convenience — pickNurse() ranks nurses by distance
# from the patient, so a patient with no latitude makes every nurse score the
# same and the nearest-nurse dispatch silently stops working.
#
# TWO SEPARATE KEYS, on purpose:
#
# 1. Server key — SECRET. Used by /api/geocode for search and reverse lookup.
#    Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create API key
#    Enable:    "Places API (New)"  and  "Geocoding API"
#    Restrict:  Application restrictions → IP addresses (your server's IP)
#               API restrictions → the two APIs above only
# GOOGLE_MAPS_SERVER_KEY=""
#
# 2. Browser key — PUBLIC, readable by anyone viewing the page. Renders the map
#    only. Must be referrer-restricted or it can be spent by strangers.
#    Enable:    "Maps JavaScript API"
#    Restrict:  Application restrictions → HTTP referrers (your domains,
#               e.g. http://localhost:3000/*  and  https://yourdomain.com/*)
#               API restrictions → Maps JavaScript API only
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY=""
# The address map's pin needs a Map ID. Empty uses Google's DEMO_MAP_ID,
# which is fine for development. For production create one (free):
# Google Cloud → Google Maps Platform → Map Management → Create Map ID
# (type JavaScript, Vector), and put it here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=""

# ── Online payment: Razorpay (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Without these two keys online payment is simply off: patients book without
# paying and clinics record bank transfers, exactly as before.
#
# With them:
#   - a patient pays the drip price to book a session (or hold a slot), and is
#     refunded automatically, in full, when it does not go ahead — a physician
#     declines, the team or a clinic cancels, vitals stop it, a held slot lapses.
#     Cancelling inside the late window refunds all but the late fee; moving
#     inside it asks for the fee first.
#   - a clinic pays an order online (received at once — nobody has to check it),
#     or still records a transfer; an order paid online and then cancelled is
#     refunded automatically.
#   - a clinic on credit pays each invoice online from Billing.
#   - admins see every payment and refund under Admin → Payments, can refund by
#     hand, and are told when a refund fails.
#
# 1. Keys — Razorpay Dashboard → Account & Settings → API Keys → Generate.
#    Test keys start rzp_test_ (no real money moves; use Razorpay's test cards
#    and UPI id success@razorpay). Live keys start rzp_live_ and need the
#    account's KYC activated. The key id is public (it is sent to the browser to
#    open Checkout); the secret never leaves the server.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=""
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=""
#
# 2. Webhook — Dashboard → Account & Settings → Webhooks → Add New Webhook:
#      URL     https://<your domain>/api/payments/webhook
#      Secret  any long random string; put the same one here
#      Events  payment.captured, payment.failed, order.paid,
#              refund.processed, refund.failed
#    It is the safety net for a patient who closes the page at the wrong moment
#    and it is how "refund processed" reaches people. Payments still confirm
#    without it (the page, and a check on every payment screen, ask Razorpay
#    directly), but set it up before going live. On a laptop, Razorpay cannot
#    reach localhost: use a tunnel (ngrok, cloudflared) to test it.
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
#
# 3. Capture — Dashboard → Account & Settings → Payment Capture: set automatic
#    capture. (If it is left manual, the app captures each payment itself.)
#
# Optional: "optimum" asks Razorpay for instant refunds (usually within
# minutes) where the bank supports it, falling back to normal where it cannot;
# Razorpay charges per instant refund, and the account may need the feature
# enabled. "normal" (the default) is free and takes 5–7 working days.
# RAZORPAY_REFUND_SPEED="normal"

# kie.ai API key. Only needed if you want scroll-craft to GENERATE imagery and
# text.
KIE_AI_API_KEY=
